# Stack

Vue 3 + TypeScript on Vite. Style with Tailwind CSS v4 and daisyUI 5. The only theme is `discovery` in `src/style.css`.

## Package manager

Use pnpm for every install and script. The lockfile is `pnpm-lock.yaml`.

```bash
pnpm install
pnpm add <pkg>
pnpm add -D <pkg>
pnpm dev
pnpm test
pnpm build
```

## Layout

- UI: `src/components` and `src/views`, as `<script setup lang="ts">` SFCs
- Session state: `src/composables`
- Domain logic: plain `.ts` modules (`src/scoring`, `src/prompt`, `src/flow`, `src/data`, `src/export`)
- Tests: Vitest files named `*.test.ts` beside the module they cover

Check types and produce a build with `pnpm build` (`vue-tsc -b && vite build`). Run unit tests with `pnpm test`.

## UI

Use a daisyUI component class before writing CSS. Use Tailwind utilities for layout and spacing. Add a `<style>` block or a rule in `src/style.css` only when daisyUI and Tailwind have no class for that job.

```vue
<button type="button" class="btn btn-primary">Continue</button>
```

## Practices

- Composition API with typed `defineProps` and `defineEmits`. Keep SFCs presentational; put scoring, prompts, and flow in `.ts` modules.
- Name values for what they represent. Give each function one job. Reuse an existing component or composable before adding another.
- Semantic HTML: associate a label with every control, set `type` on buttons, and keep keyboard focus visible.
- Strict TypeScript: annotate public types, skip `any`, and model variants as string unions.
